## Bug Description
When processing a malformed SUCI during UE registration, the AMF attempts to access invalid array indices, resulting in a runtime panic.
This issue occurs during malformed SUCI parsing in nasType.(*MobileIdentity5GS).GetSUCI when both the PLMN identifier is invalid and the length fields are inconsistent. The SUCI parsing logic attempted to access array indices that don't exist (index out of range [-1]). The panic disrupts the AMF service, leaves resources unreleased, and prevents legitimate user registrations.

## To Reproduce
1. Start the AMF and ensure it is ready to process a UE registration request.
2. Initiate an NGAP registration request containing malformed SUCI data:
